 "title": "PwC CEO's Corporate Ladder Secret",
 "topic": "business ideas",
 "summary": "This video discusses how Paul Griggs went from an intern to the CEO of PwC over a 28-year journey. The creator claims the ultimate secret to climbing the corporate ladder is working on the weekends.",
 "key_points": [
  "Paul Griggs spent 28 years at PwC going from intern to CEO.",
  "Employee A logs off on Friday and enjoys the weekend.",
  "Employee B spends Saturday and Sunday reading reports, researching clients, and working hard.",
  "On Monday, Employee B appears much more prepared.",
  "Doing this every weekend for 28 years can help someone become CEO."
 ],
 "content": "The CEO of PwC went from being an intern all the way to CEO. And during that 28-year journey, he learned the ultimate secret to climbing the corporate ladder: working on the weekends. Now, let's compare two employees. Employee A logged off on Friday, went to see his friends, and enjoyed his weekend. Employee B spent all of Saturday and Sunday reading reports, researching the client, and working his [unclear] off. Then, they both come back on Monday, and guess who looks more prepared? I think the answer is pretty obvious. Now, do that every weekend for 28 years and you too can become CEO. The great spirit of the Church of Work is truly alive here. [unclear].",
